From 0a9ceae7b36ae6b4e555770d5a582070fa666792 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Fri, 15 May 2026 16:44:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] perf phase 11 patch 0150 -- wave-54 PERF_MODE infra + cut A2
 (pin-backdrop)

Per flush-instr's docs/internal/PHASE11-WAVE-54-CONTRACT.md. Wave-54 is
the first wave of the 50 Hz program's Track A (Performance Mode) --
50HZ-CONSOLIDATED-PLAN.md sec.3. ONE mechanism, one patch: the
PERF_MODE level toggle (inert alone) + cut A2 (pin-backdrop), which is
A2's only consumer.

WHY DOS NEEDS THIS: Cave Story is authored at GAME_FPS=50 but the
faithful render is measured-closed at ~30 fps on g2k (Pentium-OD-83 /
Cirrus CL-GD5434) -- the gap is bounded by the 33 MHz memory bus, fixed
silicon. The 50 Hz program trades render fidelity for raw fps behind an
opt-in toggle while the faithful default stays untouched. PERF_MODE=0
(or unset) -> every cut gate is false -> the binary is byte-identical
to current production (the wave-53 line); this is the load-bearing
correctness invariant.

PERF_MODE INFRA (contract sec.1.1):
- SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_PERF_MODE -- integer level 0/1/2 (0=faithful
  default / 1=smooth / 2=fast; cumulative).
- perf_mode_level() in map.cpp: sentinel-cached int, resolved + clamped
  once on first call (the wave-53 skip_redundant_clear_enabled() /
  wave-46 OPL3 hint-cache idiom). NO per-flip getenv (wave-38 hazard).
  Unknown/malformed env -> std::atoi yields 0 -> faithful. Per-frame
  cost is a cached int compare.
- Wave-54 wires level>=1 to cut A2 only. Level 2 parses + clamps but
  gates nothing yet -- B2 (wave-55) and D (wave-56+) fill it.
- Unlike the default-ON levers (bg-skip / mds-clear-LUT / skip-
  redundant-clear), PERF_MODE defaults to 0 and PERF_MODE=0 IS the
  off/killswitch state -- it is an opt-in MODE, not a default-ON lever.

CUT A2 -- PIN-BACKDROP (contract sec.1.2):
In map_draw_backdrop(), when perf_mode_level() >= 1 and the map's
scrolltype is BK_PARALLAX or BK_FOLLOWFG, the backdrop is drawn as
BK_FIXED for that frame: parscroll pins to 0,0. That pins the only
frame-varying component of the patch-0080/0126 backdrop-tile-loop cache
key, so the key goes frame-invariant -> the cache HITS every scrolling
frame -> the per-frame parallax RE-RENDER is elided. The cache->window
blit floor remains (the wave-54 matrix measures the re-render-vs-blit
split directly). On static frames wave-48 bg-skip (patch 0143) already
elides the backdrop entirely, so A2's addressable cost is the scrolling
frames only.

NX-AUTHOR-1 (contract sec.1.2, contract-of-record version after the
nx-engine STOP-and-ack narrowing, flush-instr-acked): the effective
scrolltype is a LOCAL that drives ONLY the switch -- never a persistent
map.scrolltype mutation. Other code reads map.scrolltype
(map_clear_is_redundant() switches on it; save/load; map reload). The
backdrop cache-key store AND compare are left reading map.scrolltype /
map.parscroll_* unchanged: map.scrolltype is per-map invariant so
store==compare holds, and the pin reaches the key via the parscroll
component alone. Swapping only the compare side to the effective value
would create a permanent store/compare mismatch -> permanent cache miss
-> A2 collapse; that is why the literal scrolltype key field is not
touched.

BK_FASTLEFT / BK_FASTLEFT_LAYERS / NOFALLLEFT are explicitly NOT pinned
-- their scroll is an intentional gameplay effect (Ironhead auto-
scroll); pinning would freeze it (visual breakage, not a fidelity
trade). BK_FIXED / BK_HIDE* are already fixed / self-clearing.

CORRECTNESS: at PERF_MODE=0 the local eff_scrolltype equals
map.scrolltype, so map_draw_backdrop() is bit-identical to the patch-
0149 original -- build-qa ImageMagick AE=0 vs the wave-53 baseline is
the gate. PERF_MODE=1's pinned backdrop (the backdrop stops parallax-
scrolling) IS the feature, not a regression.

BANNERS for tests/run-gameplay-smoke.sh BANNERS array:
"perf-mode: level=[0-2]"            (emitted on first perf_mode_level())
"perf-mode A2: backdrop pinned"     (emitted on first actual A2 convert)

FILES: src/map.h (perf_mode_level decl), src/map.cpp (perf_mode_level
helper + the A2 eff_scrolltype gate in map_draw_backdrop).
---
 src/map.cpp | 87 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 src/map.h   | 12 ++++++++
 2 files changed, 98 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/map.cpp b/src/map.cpp
index ddc7305..dfc8b86 100644
--- a/src/map.cpp
+++ b/src/map.cpp
@@ -775,6 +775,44 @@ bool skip_redundant_clear_enabled()
   return g_skip_redundant_clear == 1;
 }
 
+// DOS-PORT (patch 0150, Phase 11 wave-54 -- Track A Performance Mode,
+// PHASE11-WAVE-54-CONTRACT.md sec.1.1): cached level toggle for the
+// opt-in fidelity-reduction mode. SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_PERF_MODE is an
+// integer 0/1/2 (0=faithful default / 1=smooth / 2=fast; cumulative).
+//
+// WHY DOS NEEDS THIS: Cave Story is authored at GAME_FPS=50 but the
+// faithful render is measured-closed at ~30 fps on g2k (Pentium-OD-83
+// / Cirrus 5434). The 50 Hz program's Track A trades render fidelity
+// for raw fps behind this opt-in toggle; the faithful path stays the
+// untouched production default. PERF_MODE=0/unset -> every cut gate is
+// false -> the binary is byte-identical to current production.
+//
+// Sentinel-cached on first call (the wave-53 skip_redundant_clear_
+// enabled() / wave-46 OPL3 idiom) -- NO per-flip getenv (wave-38
+// hazard). Wave-54 wires level>=1 to cut A2 (pin-backdrop); level 2
+// parses + clamps but gates nothing until wave-55+ (B2 / D). Unknown
+// or malformed env -> atoi yields 0 -> faithful. First call emits the
+// build-qa BANNERS-grep banner.
+static int g_perf_mode = -1;  // -1 undecided / 0 faithful / 1 / 2
+int perf_mode_level()
+{
+  if (g_perf_mode < 0)
+  {
+    const char *e = std::getenv("SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_PERF_MODE");
+    int v = e ? std::atoi(e) : 0;
+    if (v < 0)
+      v = 0;
+    if (v > 2)
+      v = 2;  // clamp; unknown/malformed -> 0 via atoi
+    g_perf_mode = v;
+    LOG_INFO("perf-mode: level={} ({})", g_perf_mode,
+             g_perf_mode == 0   ? "faithful (default)"
+             : g_perf_mode == 1 ? "smooth -- Tier 1 cuts"
+                                : "fast -- Tier 1 + Tier 2 cuts");
+  }
+  return g_perf_mode;
+}
+
 // DOS-PORT (patch 0149, Phase 11 wave-53 lever 3): skip-clear predicate.
 // Returns true (DrawScene's clearScreen(BLACK) may be skipped) iff the
 // backdrop pass will provably repaint EVERY screen row this frame, so
@@ -1425,7 +1463,54 @@ void map_draw_backdrop(void)
   // map_backdrop_invalidate_skip_state() instead.
   map_backdrop_record_present_success();
 
-  switch (map.scrolltype)
+  // DOS-PORT (patch 0150, Phase 11 wave-54 -- Track A cut A2,
+  // pin-backdrop; PHASE11-WAVE-54-CONTRACT.md sec.1.2): when
+  // PERF_MODE>=1, treat a scrolling full-screen backdrop (BK_PARALLAX
+  // / BK_FOLLOWFG) as BK_FIXED for THIS draw. The BK_FIXED case body
+  // pins parscroll to 0,0; that pins the only frame-varying component
+  // of the 0080/0126 backdrop-tile-loop cache key, so the key goes
+  // frame-invariant and the cache HITS every scrolling frame -- the
+  // per-frame parallax RE-RENDER is elided (the cache->window blit
+  // floor remains). On static frames wave-48 bg-skip (patch 0143)
+  // already elides the backdrop entirely; A2's addressable cost is the
+  // scrolling frames only.
+  //
+  // NX-AUTHOR-1 (contract sec.1.2, contract-of-record version, ack'd
+  // by flush-instr): the effective scrolltype is a LOCAL that drives
+  // ONLY the switch below -- never a persistent map.scrolltype
+  // mutation. Other code reads map.scrolltype (map_clear_is_redundant()
+  // switches on it; save/load; map reload). The cache-key store AND
+  // compare are deliberately left reading map.scrolltype / map.parscroll_*
+  // unchanged: map.scrolltype is per-map invariant so store==compare
+  // holds, and the pin reaches the key through the parscroll component
+  // alone. Swapping only the compare side to the effective value would
+  // create a permanent store/compare mismatch -> permanent cache miss
+  // -> A2 collapse; this is why the literal value is NOT touched.
+  //
+  // BK_FASTLEFT / BK_FASTLEFT_LAYERS / NOFALLLEFT are NOT pinned --
+  // their scroll is an intentional gameplay effect (Ironhead
+  // auto-scroll); pinning would freeze it (visual breakage, not a
+  // fidelity trade). BK_FIXED / BK_HIDE* are already fixed / self-
+  // clearing -- untouched. PERF_MODE=0 -> eff == map.scrolltype -> this
+  // function is bit-identical to the patch-0149 original.
+  int eff_scrolltype = map.scrolltype;
+  if (perf_mode_level() >= 1 &&
+      (map.scrolltype == BK_PARALLAX || map.scrolltype == BK_FOLLOWFG))
+  {
+    eff_scrolltype = BK_FIXED;
+    // One banner per process, on the first frame A2 actually converts
+    // a draw -- the runtime witness that the cut is REACHED, not just
+    // embedded (strings|grep proves embed only).
+    static bool s_a2_banner_done = false;
+    if (!s_a2_banner_done)
+    {
+      s_a2_banner_done = true;
+      LOG_INFO("perf-mode A2: backdrop pinned (BK_PARALLAX/FOLLOWFG -> "
+               "BK_FIXED; parscroll 0,0 -- parallax re-render elided)");
+    }
+  }
+
+  switch (eff_scrolltype)
   {
     case BK_FIXED:
       map.parscroll_x = 0;
